feat(style-profile): real Style Profile Builder in Devs + fix CLI model detection

CLI detection:
- Claude: hardcoded aliases (opus/sonnet/haiku + [1m] variants), plus reads
  ~/.claude/settings.json to surface user's configured model; claude --help
  scraped only for full 'claude-<family>-<n>-<m>' patterns to avoid sweeping
  up plugin names and section headings
- Codex: hardcoded known ids (gpt-5.5, 5.4, 5.4-mini, 5.3-codex, 5.2) since
  codex has no models-list subcommand; reads ~/.codex/config.toml top-level
  model line to highlight user's configured default
- All providers: CLI invocation now pipes prompt via stdin with -p/--print
  mode (claude), codex exec -, gemini -p -

Style Profile Builder (user-level, outside competition pipeline):
- New APIs:
    POST /api/style-profile/upload       multipart PDFs, extracts text,
                                         stores with competition_id=null,
                                         file_role=style_profile_source
    POST /api/style-profile/generate     queues agent_run with null pipeline,
                                         builder skill + source texts as inputs
    GET  /api/style-profile              returns sources + profile + versions
    DELETE /api/style-profile/sources/[id]
- run-execution: competitionId now string|null; applyWriteFile uses
  profile-assets bucket + {userId}/style path when not scoped to competition
- pipeline-bootstrap: ensureStyleBuilderUserAgent lazy-provisions a user_agent
  in Essay compartment, seeds initial skill version from the template
- UI: DevsScreen Style Builder tab replaced by real StyleBuilderWorkspace
  with PDF uploader, source list, inline model picker, generate button,
  live token stream via Realtime, profile viewer + version history
